\ nqueens — port of pyperformance bm_nqueens.
\ Brute-force enumeration of all permutations of [0..N-1] (using recursive
\ in-place swaps) and counting those that satisfy the diagonal constraint
\ |BOARD[i] - BOARD[j]| != |i - j| for all i < j. The permutation property
\ guarantees rows/columns; the diagonal check is the only validity test.

8 constant queens
45 constant loops

variable solutions
variable board

: bswap ( a b -- )
  | a b |
  board a @i
  board a  board b @i  !i drop
  board b  rot         !i drop ;
inline

: valid? ( -- flag )
  -1 to ok
  0 queens 1 - 1 do i
    i f1+ queens 1 do j
      board i @i  board j @i  -  abs   j i -  =  not   ok and to ok
      ok not if leave then
    loop
    ok not if leave then
  loop
  ok ;

: permute
  | start ^solutions |
  start queens 1 - = if
    valid? if  f++ solutions  then
  else
    start queens 1 do i
      start i bswap
      start f1+ permute
      start i bswap
    loop
  then ;

: nqueens-run ^board ^solutions |
  now to t0
  0 loops 1 do rep
     0 queens array-of to board
     0 queens 1 do i  board i i !i drop  loop
     0 to solutions
     0 permute
  loop
  "elapsed: " . now t0 - . "s" . cr
  "solutions: " . solutions . cr ;

nqueens-run
bye
